<title>SOUTH KOREA: Shindongbang seeks 50,000T of Brazilian soybean.</title>
<headline>Shindongbang seeks 50,000T of Brazilian soybean.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shindongbang Corp, South Korea's largest edible oil producer, would buy 50,000 tonnes of Brazilian soybean for shipment between July and August, a senior company official said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The official said the company would buy the soybeans at a basis price over September futures on the Chicago Board of Trade.</p>
<p>Arrival was slated for the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>-- Seoul newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
